If you're saying that the Highlander level would strip away the skill
and judgement of normal nethack and replace it with an idiotic
life-or-death dice-rolling competition, then I agree. That's my
intention. Remember it wouldn't be compulsory for ascension, and as I
understand it there is little else that can pose a serious threat to a
well-seasoned and well-prepared player in the mid/late game. The vast
majority of players would (I imagine) avoid the Highlander level like
the plague, but every now and then you'd get someone who is
temporarily overtaken by insanity or boredom, gives it a go and gets
slaughtered meaninglessly, thus flushing however many hours of
gameplay time down the pan. The point is that unless that player had
never heard of the Highlander level (and a few warnings to it in
cookies and the opening parts of the level would be a good idea), it
would be their own damn fault. "YASD: I had a level 19 samurai with
AC-42 and then for some reason I sent him on the highlander level. I'm
still kicking myself now."

The challenge of the highlander level is resisting the temptation to
try it in the first place.


